  "namedChanges": [
    "in each file the imports are replaced by imports of the peers `base-record`, `description-parts-model`, `lws-records`, `lws-vault-sets`, `plan-links-model`, `vault-origin-rule`, `@tanstack/react-query` and this unit's own files; `entityDisplayName.ts` keeps its one import line (`./partyName`)",
    "in `recordCaches.ts` the word `export` is added in front of `flattenRecordPages`, `emptyPage`, `setList`, `upsert` and `setRecordReads`, private in the app (`recordHooks.ts:1291`, `:1797`, `:1851`, `:1878`, `:2949`) and used by the hooks of the next unit",
    "in `planFind.ts` line 371 `[\"plan-find\", vaultId]` is `planFindVaultKey(vaultId)`; in `planSearch.ts` line 26 `[\"plan-search\", planVault]` is `planSearchKey(planVault)`; the new file `cacheKeys.ts` is the one definition of `STAKEHOLDER_SEARCH_AUTHORITY_KEY`, `planSearchKey` and `planFindVaultKey` (later sites: `PlanStakeholders.tsx:920`, `PlanFunctionForm.tsx:1468`, `PlanDescriptionParts.tsx:997`, `PlanTagLinks.tsx:58`)",
    "in `partyName.ts` line 33 the text of the field `source` of `PARTY_NAME_FLOOR` (a host and an internal ruling name) is reworded; no code reads the field",
    "`GridRecord`, `asGrid` and `recordTag` are imported from `base-record`, `description-parts-model` and `plan-links-model` (equal to the app's, comments stripped) and not copied",
    "comments that name a host, a person or an internal ruling are reworded; no code changed",
    "0.2.0: `src/index.ts` exports `entityDisplayName` and `withCanonicalLabel` from `./entityDisplayName`; `withCanonicalLabel` (source lines 262-310) is copied with no code change",
    "0.3.0: in `planSearch.ts` the source import `import { fetchMainTagsForRows } from \"./recordTags\";` (source line 12) is `import { fetchMainTagsForRows } from \"@kaigilb/gilbplatformcode-main-tag\";`, a peer: the app function is the unit `main-tag`, read directly (`searchPlanRecords` is a plain function that already receives the query client, so there is no host object)",
    "0.3.0: `needsMainTag` (source lines 175-183, between `factTrim` and `displayFriendly`) is not copied: it lives in the unit `main-tag`, which this unit imports, so a copy here would be a second home (and `main-tag` cannot import it back from here without a cycle); the source range 170-197 is taken as its moved part, 185-212"
  ],
